        "original_id": "2b98ce32-895f-534d-b466-d5a51ef412f4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: York, England, Brentwood, Essex, Northern Europe\n- Organizations: York Minster, The Cathedral and Metropolitical Church of Saint Peter in York, Brentwood Cathedral, The Cathedral of St Mary and St Helen\n- People: John Farr Abbott\n- Topics: Cathedrals, burial\n\nFacts:\n- York Minster, formally called The Cathedral and Metropolitical Church of Saint Peter in York, is the cathedral of York in England.\n- York Minster is one of the largest cathedrals of its kind in Northern Europe.\n- Brentwood Cathedral, formally called The Cathedral of St Mary and St Helen, is the Roman Catholic cathedral in Brentwood, Essex.\n- John Farr Abbott died in York.\n- John Farr Abbott is buried in York Minster.",
